From b2256cb666340209011f4a344d9971030ab98e2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuk3s <44327449+nuk3s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:18:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kv-offload): bound the total time of a disk transfer

Upstream base: the patch applies to local-inference-lab/vllm at
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the 702 patches of
spark-ds41f-1120 (candidate-62, 0001 to 0829) and patches 9030 to 9040
of this series.

Rationale: with the progress check alone, a disk that completes one slot
every few seconds held a load, and every load queued behind it, for
hours without a fault. This patch also fails a disk transfer that runs
longer than disk_io_timeout_s plus disk_io_slot_budget_s for each of its
slots, counted from the moment the IO thread took it from the queue,
however steady its progress. The progress check stays and runs first.
The new kv_connector_extra_config key disk_io_slot_budget_s defaults to
0.02 s. On three DGX Spark nodes a restore of 1,959 slots took 0.53 to
0.55 ms a slot while 2 and 4 other streams were decoding, which is about
36 times under that budget (experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier/README.md).
The running transfer of each IO thread is now a RunningTransfer record
with the event, the start, the last progress, and the slot count, and a
transfer that an IO thread takes from the queue after a fault no longer
leaves a stale running record behind.

Quality implications: the patch does not change outputs.

Tests: on the CPU path the offload suite passed 188 tests, with 2
CUDA-only modules skipped. In the new tests, a store of 12 slots at
0.06 s a write under a 0.3 s timeout does not degrade the tier, a load of
12 slots at 0.1 s a read fails at its bound of 0.54 s, and the load
queued behind that slow load fails with no I/O. Another test checks that
a load taken from the queue after a fault leaves no running transfer.
The CUDA path of a transfer that reaches the bound was not tested, and
no transfer reached the bound during the hardware run.

Upstream status: the patch is proposed to spark-ds41f in
experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier and has not been submitted to
local-inference-lab/vllm.
